<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Giustiniani family</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Giustiniani were a Genoese family association formed in 1362 by the shareholders of the Maona of Chios, who took the common surname and governed the island of Chios and its mastic trade until the Ottoman conquest of 1566. Its members included <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giovanni-giustiniani-longo">Giovanni Giustiniani Longo</a>, who commanded the defence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> in 1453, and later cardinals and bankers in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/giustiniani-family.jpg" alt="Giustiniani family" width="320" height="223" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Didier Descouens · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:(Venice)_Palazzo_Giustinian.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
